From b06c85e708be142b1475f88a6dd665c23b15f7dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicole@muzz.in>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 03:58:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] svg: presentation attributes in the cascade; root sizing from
 the viewBox

Presentation attributes (fill="white") are parsed as their CSS property
when set and enter the cascade as presentational hints, so an author rule
overrides them even when it sets the value the element would inherit
(The Verge's logo). var() keeps working in them.

The serializer hook becomes an attribute rewrite. With a viewBox it drops
the root's width/height, whose partial presence (width without height)
gave the rasterizer the wrong natural size and shrank icons (Booking).
Declarations are appended to inline style, and inline-named paint
properties re-emitted computed. viewBox parsing accepts decimals.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
